add('F1','Shared mechanics for standing checks','Provide only file ownership/discovery, local process invocation and the-way result recording; keep expectations and adopted rule lists out of shared mechanics. A failed tool invocation produces a failure with no invariant verdict, never a pass. Discover tracked and unignored new product files by current part ownership, excluding dependencies, generated output, submodule and run records.', ['scripts/quality_support.py','tests/quality/test_quality_support.py'],['.the-way/gate/run_tests.py','.the-way/gate/README.md','tests/invariants/test_application_package_layout.py'], 'Start with tests for new nested owned files, ambiguous ownership, missing executable, malformed output, nonzero process result and record schema. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_quality_support.py`. No network or tool download in checks.','Foundation entries and map')
add('F2','ESLint source and configuration checks','Implement the methods for settlements 15 and 18 from their sentences and methods alone, including exact adopted active rules/options, TS and JS coverage, TS6 parser API, inline suppressions and changed configuration. Keep independently captured expected membership in the check, not imported from configuration being tested.', ['scripts/check_eslint.py','scripts/inspect_eslint.mjs','tests/quality/test_eslint_checks.py'],['.the-way/product-guidelines/coding/template.md','tsconfig.browser.json','tsconfig.server.json'], 'Start with isolated fixture tests for new TS/JS files, config disabling or weakening a rule, adding exclusions, inline directives and tool failures; run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_eslint_checks.py`. Run `python -B scripts/check_eslint.py --record .runs/eslint.jsonl` and `python -B scripts/check_eslint.py --configuration --record .runs/eslint-configuration.jsonl`; missing installed tools/config at this stage is an expected genuine non-pass, not an expected-pass test.','F1; settlements 2, 11, 12, 15, 18')
add('F3','Python and Bash standing checks','Implement settlement 16 with the explicit adopted 393-rule list, isolated Ruff configuration and suppression detection limited to blocking rules; implement settlement 17 with the pinned ShellCheck default nonoptional Bash set, every severity, no external rc/environment changes and source directive protection. Detect new owned files, including extensionless standalone Bash scripts.', ['scripts/check_ruff.py','scripts/check_shellcheck.py','tests/quality/test_python_shell_checks.py'],['.the-way/product-guidelines/coding/template.md','deploy/loop2-deploy'], 'Start with new-path, suppression, nonblocking noqa:E402, environment override and missing-tool fixtures. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_python_shell_checks.py`; run `python -B scripts/check_ruff.py --record .runs/ruff.jsonl` and `python -B scripts/check_shellcheck.py --record .runs/shellcheck.jsonl`, retaining expected absent-tool results until Slice 2.','F1; settlements 3, 4, 13, 14, 16, 17')
add('F4','Formatting standing check','Implement settlement 19 using local pinned Prettier with the editor configuration, full part-derived TS/JS and browser HTML/CSS scope, new paths, LF bytes and configuration-only changes reaching the check. Check expected adopted configuration rather than accepting an arbitrary formatter invocation.', ['scripts/check_format.py','tests/quality/test_format_check.py'],['.the-way/product-guidelines/coding/template.md','.gitattributes'], 'Start with good/bad new-path fixtures, excluded files, weakened config, CRLF and unavailable tool. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_format_check.py` and `python -B scripts/check_format.py --record .runs/format.jsonl`; before installation and complete reformatting record the actual non-pass.','F1; settlements 5, 19')
add('F5','Dependency audit of introduced versions','Implement settlement 20 as its own reviewable change: compare every build-tools npm manifest/lockfile against explicit fork point; use real package-name/version pairs including aliases and nested, transitive, dev, optional and peer dependencies; match advisory ranges to those exact versions through pinned npm. Unchanged pairs do not block, empty newly introduced set can pass offline only after complete valid comparison, and unsupported/incomplete/error data produces no successful verdict. External data is untrusted.', ['scripts/check_dependencies.py','tests/quality/test_dependency_audit.py'],['.the-way/product-guidelines/coding/template.md','package.json','package-lock.json'], 'Start with deterministic fixture tests covering changed version vs unchanged vulnerable version, aliases, multiple installed versions, direct/transitive/dev/optional/peer packages, nested new manifests/locks, missing base/locks, unsupported lock/report shape, range matching and all severities, network errors and offline no-change. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_dependency_audit.py`; run `python -B scripts/check_dependencies.py --fork-point '+base+' --record .runs/dependency-audit.jsonl`. Live result is not replaced by fixture success.','F1; settlement 6, 20')
add('F6','Reliable existing process observations','Through the foundation route for modified invariant tests, reject failed process reads in both Windows and Unix branches of the existing serving-process check, and remove the accepted unused API-check import. Retain the invariant sentences and independently test the observation mechanics; the support cleanup change waits for Slice 3.', ['tests/invariants/test_loop2_one_serving_process.py','tests/invariants/test_loop2_api_error_route.py','tests/quality/test_process_observation.py'],['tests/invariants/loop2_invariant_support.py'], 'Write failing mocked subprocess tests first: valid-looking stdout with nonzero exit must be rejected on both platforms. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_process_observation.py`; run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/invariants -p test_loop2_one_serving_process.py` and `python -m unittest discover -s tests/invariants -p test_loop2_api_error_route.py`; reserve the original check author and full independent acceptance route if any invariant method interpretation changes.','Foundation route for invariant test changes; independent of F1-F5')
add('1','Install npm tools and preserve TS7 compilation','Declare and lock all accepted npm tools, including pinned local npm; use the accepted TS6 API alias plus separate TS7 compiler alias and explicit compiler path. Configure ESLint and Prettier as settled, cover new part-owned files and new check code, keep one application npm package. Add narrow LF attributes only for Prettier scope and document local setup.', ['package.json','package-lock.json','scripts/build.mjs','eslint.config.mjs','prettier.config.mjs','.gitattributes','README.md'],['tsconfig.browser.json','tsconfig.server.json','Dockerfile','.the-way/product-guidelines/coding/template.md'], 'Run `npm ci`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and configuration check `python -B scripts/check_eslint.py --configuration --record .runs/eslint-configuration.jsonl`. Verify installed exact versions and TS7 compiler execution, not just aliases in JSON. Run source/format standing checks and retain outstanding baseline failures until their slices; run the audit with the explicit base. Do not silently weaken rule count or choose replacement versions.','F1-F5; settlements 1, 2, 5, 6 and map')
add('2','Install local Python-distributed tools','Declare Ruff and the ShellCheck wrapper in a dedicated requirements input and fully hashed lock, with no runtime dependencies missing from the lock. Install into a repository-local ignored environment under .runs; wrapper package version is an implementation detail and executed ShellCheck must report the exact accepted binary version. Describe repeatable installation and executable locations in existing README.', ['requirements-quality.in','requirements-quality.txt','README.md'],['.gitignore','.the-way/product-guidelines/coding/template.md'], 'Create local environment using `python -m venv .runs/quality-venv`; install with `.runs/quality-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-quality.txt` on Windows (use the environment bin path on Unix). Verify executable versions. Run `python -B scripts/check_ruff.py --record .runs/ruff.jsonl` and `python -B scripts/check_shellcheck.py --record .runs/shellcheck.jsonl`; Ruff baseline findings remain until Slice 3. No downloads occur in either check.','Slice 1 (README); F3; settlements 3, 4 and map')
add('3','Clean up test-server resources on failures','Remove the remaining two accepted unused imports, close stdout if stderr opening fails, close both logs and remove temporary resources if spawning fails, preserve logs for a live server, and still attempt to terminate the known main process when child enumeration fails. Reject failed enumeration output. Do not widen Python cleanup beyond the eight accepted findings without returning evidence.', ['tests/invariants/loop2_invariant_support.py','tests/deploy/test_loop2_deploy_build.py','tests/quality/test_invariant_support.py'],['tests/invariants/test_loop2_one_serving_process.py','tests/invariants/test_loop2_api_error_route.py'], 'Write meaningful failure-injection tests first for second open, spawn, failed descendant query with partial stdout, main-process termination and stop without a fully initialized process. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests/quality -p test_invariant_support.py`, `python -B .the-way/gate/run_tests.py tests/invariants --record .runs/invariants-after-support.jsonl`, `python -B .the-way/gate/run_tests.py tests/deploy --record .runs/deploy-after-support.jsonl`, and Ruff check. Preserve environment-related unrun results.','F6; Slice 2; settlement 16')
add('4','Fix simulation assertions and format modules','Remove only the fifteen accepted unnecessary simulation assertions, preserve necessary ones, and format the seven simulation modules with adopted Prettier. Game behavior remains unchanged.', ['src/browser/sim/'+p+'.ts' for p in ['game','hex','layout','program','random','run','types']],['tests/sim/hex.test.mjs','tests/sim/layout.test.mjs','tests/sim/program.test.mjs','tests/sim/time.test.mjs'], 'Run local pinned Prettier on exactly the Change paths, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and `node --test "tests/sim/*.test.mjs"`. Verify emitted behavior/AST changes are limited to removal of assertions plus formatting; use existing simulation invariants and compare assertion removal count against the task. Run ESLint check, retaining the one view finding until Slice 7.','Slice 1; settlements 8, 15, 19')
add('5','Format game content data','Format the six current content-data files and preserve all data and exported identifiers.', ['src/browser/sim/data/'+p+'.ts' for p in ['actions','archetypes','balance','conditions','maps','resources']],['tests/sim/data.test.mjs'], 'Run local pinned Prettier on the Change paths, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `node --test tests/sim/data.test.mjs`, and current content-identifiers/simulation-isolation checks. Verify only formatting changed.','Slice 1; settlements 7, 19')
add('6','Format view control construction','Format the first five view modules without intended UI or behavior changes.', ['src/browser/view/'+p+'.ts' for p in ['app','clock','credits','footer','program-editor']],['tests/view/program-editor.test.mjs','tests/view/icons.test.mjs'], 'Run local pinned Prettier on the Change paths, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and `node --test "tests/view/*.test.mjs"`. Check normalized syntax/token content is unchanged and preserve string literals.','Slice 1; settlements 9, 19')
add('7','Fix terrain assertion and format remaining browser files','Remove the one accepted terrain-picture assertion; format remaining view modules, browser entry and HTML while preserving behavior and rendered appearance.', ['src/browser/view/'+p+'.ts' for p in ['send-panel','status-row','terrain-panel','terrain-picture','tile-list']]+['src/browser/main.ts','src/browser/index.html'],['tests/view/terrain-picture.test.mjs','tests/view/status-row.test.mjs','tests/view/tile-list.test.mjs'], 'Run local pinned Prettier on Change paths, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `node --test "tests/view/*.test.mjs"`, and ESLint check. Confirm cumulative removal count is exactly sixteen and no other assertion was removed; inspect HTML whitespace effects and token preservation. Any discovered visible behavior change returns to root before continuing.','Slice 4 (cumulative assertion completion); Slice 1; settlements 9, 15, 19')
add('8','Format HTTP server and integration tests','Format the server application, its entry point and the two HTTP/startup tests, preserving server routing, process startup and assertions.', ['src/server/app.ts','src/server/main.ts','tests/http.test.mjs','tests/startup.test.mjs'],['tests/invariants/test_loop2_api_error_route.py','tests/invariants/test_account_server_occupied_address.py'], 'Run local pinned Prettier on Change paths, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and `node --test tests/http.test.mjs tests/startup.test.mjs`; verify normalized syntax unchanged. Apply adversarial HTTP/startup coverage already in tests because src/server is a trust boundary.','Slice 1; settlements 10, 19')
