lines+=['| File ownership and standing-check reach | part map | To do 8–9; necessary consequences of added files | F1–F6 and Slices 1–12 |','', 'Write all entries before F1. Use the project record-environment-fact, record-decision, record-invariant and update-part-map skills, in linked-entry dependency order. The task carries no MVP projected entry. Copy the exact identifiers and sentences for settlements 21–22 from the pinned general template. Give source-code linter checks both their covered parts and build-tools; the formatter additionally reaches deployment through .gitattributes. Guidelines references reach agent-workflow/product-foundation; form names every. The foundation author settles final invariant identifiers and methods and supplies their whole sentences and methods to check authors.','', 'The map gives all new scripts, requirements files, npm configuration and tests/quality files to build-tools, and guidelines/** to agent-workflow. Expand scripts/build.mjs to a nonoverlapping scripts/** assignment rather than duplicate ownership; include eslint.config.mjs, prettier.config.mjs, requirements-quality.in and requirements-quality.txt explicitly. Keep .gitattributes assigned to deployment. Existing invariant-test ownership stays unchanged. Follow through necessary consequence fields rather than invent new decisions or glossary terms.','', 'Foundation checks F1–F6 are bounded preparation within the foundation route, before dependent covered code. Each is a fresh check-author assignment, not ordinary authoring of the configuration it checks; F1 is mechanics only. Sentence author, check author and covered-code author must be three distinct identities. The sentence/method check handoff must not carry product-author reasoning, this plan, or a duplicate requirements catalogue; the orchestrator supplies the allowed methodological sources. No check author later owns a covered-code/configuration slice. Product slices never edit frozen invariant checks; any required correction returns to the foundation step. Existing serving-process test changes in F6 use that same route.','', '## Slices','']
