lines+=['## Independence and execution','', 'F2–F5 are theoretically independent after F1 because each owns separate methods and fixture tests; the audit has its own scope and review. F6 can be judged against its original two checks independently of new tooling. Product formatting Slices 5, 6 and 8 are separate goals after installation; Slices 9 and 10 wait for the corresponding source formatting only for coherent review/test evidence. Separate files do not authorize concurrent writers: all executions and all tests using shared ports, node_modules or the mutable worktree are sequential. Superpowers 6.4.1 subagent-driven-development independently forbids parallel implementation subagents. Root records its ruling before dispatch.','', 'Every author reads current whole applicable guidelines once they exist and refreshes the part/foundation selection before relying on it. The missing general guidelines are this task output, so earlier slices do not wait for them. There is no styleguide or intended visible UI change, hence no styleguide order example applies. Existing files created by earlier slices are additionally read before dependent work; those absent at planning time are named in dependencies rather than as nonexistent Read paths. Refresh the plan-size report if a slice expands its write set.','', 'All check commands run from the task worktree. Each full sanitized output and actual exit code is preserved in the cycle reports. No unrun check is a pass. Every slice has an independent reviewer and weakest-point check. Foundation-check baseline tool/config failures and remaining adopted-code violations are expected only until their dependent slices complete; final integration requires full compliance, with no transition-debt mechanism. Use current main commit for merge-onto at final verification, and actual original fork point for audits. Standalone script names/flags above are planned callable interfaces, to be realized by the independent method authors; if they need a different interface root updates plan/handoffs before downstream invocation.','', 'After Slice 12 root runs the full product gate, every changed part test directory, npm tests/typecheck, all new standing checks, all changed foundation format guards and both guideline checks. Capture unchanged environment limitations honestly. Whole-branch review includes final diff coverage, separate invariant deliberate breaks and good/bad cases in scratch worktrees; then return step, independent foundation assessment, reconciliation and request are cycle stages, not additional implementation slices.','', '## Coverage','', '| What the task requires | Slices or entries |','|---|---|','| Required outcome: coding guidelines with standing checks for current product | All entries; F1–F6; 1–12 |']
