lines+=['', '## Choices','', '| Choice | Way rejected | Cost if wrong |','|---|---|','| Keep invariant method work in six bounded foundation batches, independently from configuration/code authors. | Let one tooling author write the policy, its checker and covered config. | More dispatches; fewer author identities would violate WAY-69 and invalidate acceptance. |','| Use Python scripts for standing-check CLI/records and a small JS bridge only for ESLint APIs. | Mix independent record implementations across several runtimes. | Extra bridge process; common mechanics must not hide expectations or become another policy source. |','| Use a repository-local Python venv with hashed requirements for Ruff and shellcheck-py; verify the actual ShellCheck binary version. | Hand-maintain a new cross-platform archive installer or use global tools. | Wrapper is another distribution dependency; unsupported platforms must report unavailable rather than silently fall back. Metadata confirms Windows/Linux x86-64 wheels, but actual install/execution is still an implementation check. |','| Preserve accepted TS6 API and TS7 compiler using the already trialed two package aliases. | Downgrade the compiler or run ESLint against an unsupported TS7 API. | Additional package footprint is accepted by Q2; explicit compiler resolution and regression checks are needed. |','| Keep the audit in one independent method batch with adversarial fixtures and live run. | Treat npm audit exit status or highest package severity as the whole policy. | More precise parsing/range matching; unsupported shapes must be non-pass rather than guessed. |','| Group the 45 formatting targets by kind and test suite, each under ten changed files, with assertion removals in the owning source batches. | One 45-file formatting slice, or one slice per file. | Several review ranges; monolith violates size guard, per-file slices add no useful review boundary. |','| Write complete guidelines after code is compliant, then add only the AGENTS.md pointer. | Publish tables claiming copy status before repairs or duplicate commands in instructions. | Later guideline writing requires authors to apply frozen task/template until then; allowed for the task creating missing guidelines. |','| Use English for code identifiers/comments and Polish explanatory guidelines text with required English schema headings. | Add a separate language decision or duplicate bilingual documents. | Follows current repository code and user-facing documentation; schema fields remain exact. |','']
